== Features ==

=== The Mastery ===

:''Main article [[The Mastery]]''
The Mastery is unlocked with #1Ω. It gives boost based on the player's progression such as current total upgrades, cube clicks or total challenge levels.

=== Jerry ===

[[File:Jerry.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Jerry]]''
Jerry is an npc, they say the quotes and other stuff. They are unlocked with #2Ω.

=== The Stud ===

:''Main article: [[The Stud]]''
The Stud is a tower that can be grown one stud at a time by purchasing #1αb (The stud tower) up to 65,536 studs tall. This feature also existed in [[ASAP]]'s previous incremental / upgrade tree games such as NJUT (Not JJT Upgrade Tree) and EUT (Everything Upgrade Tree). {{Studs}} can be utilized to buy upgrades with {{Tag|Upgrade|NJUT}} tags. 

=== Gateway ===

[[File:The_Gateway.png|200px|thumb|right]]
Teleports the player to [[The Void]] upon going into it

=== Trampoline ===

[[File:Trampoline.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Trampoline]]
The Trampoline is a feature unlocked by upgrade #2B. It acts as a means of travel that lets the player jump to and from the Bonus Baseplate. Another trampoline is located on the Bonus Baseplate to go back to the Main Baseplate. The one on this baseplate is yellow with an outline of a yellow star on the bouncy part.

=== Cube Teleporter ===

[[File:CubeTeleporter.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Cube Teleporter]]''
The Cube teleporter is a feature unlocked by multiple upgrades. It allows the player to teleport to different zones of the game.

=== Terriac de Scripta ===

[[File:Terriac_de_Scripta.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Paper Dimension]]''
:''Terriac de Scripta&lt;br&gt; In Memoriam, Terriac Papere Orbis&lt;br&gt; - MCMXVII -''&lt;br&gt;
The text above is written in Latin which roughly translates to:&lt;br&gt;

:''Terriac the scripter&lt;br&gt; In memory of Terriac Paper World&lt;br&gt; - 1917 -''

Going into the painting teleports the player to the [[Paper Dimension]].
