== Features ==

=== The Mastery ===

:''Main article [[The Mastery]]''
'''{{Color|rgb(182, 253, 192)|The Mastery|Black}}''' is unlocked with {{Upgrade|#1Ω|X-side}}. It gives boost based on the player's progression such as current total upgrades, cube clicks or total challenge levels.

=== Jerry ===

[[File:Jerry.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Jerry]]''
Jerry is an npc, they say the quotes and other stuff. They are unlocked with {{Upgrade|#2Ω|x-side}}.

=== The Stud ===

:''Main article: [[The Stud]]''
The Stud is a tower that can be grown by purchasing {{Upgrade|#1αb|NJUT}} (The stud tower) up to 65,536 studs tall. This feature also existed in [[ASAP]]'s previous incremental / upgrade tree games such as NJUT (Not JJT Upgrade Tree) and EUT (Everything Upgrade Tree). {{Studs}} can be utilized to buy upgrades with {{Tag|Upgrade|NJUT}} tags. 

=== Gateway ===

[[File:The_Gateway.png|200px|thumb|right]]
Teleports the player to [[The Void]] upon falling into it. It is located to the right of the yellow trampoline. 

=== Trampoline ===

[[File:Trampoline.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Trampoline]]
The Trampoline is a feature unlocked by upgrade {{Upgrade|#2B|Yellow}}. It acts as a means of travel that lets the player jump to and from the {{Baseplate|Bonus}}. Another trampoline is located on the {{Baseplate|Bonus}} to go back to the {{Baseplate|Main}}. The one on this baseplate is yellow with a hollow yellow star on the jump mat.

=== Cube Teleporter ===

[[File:CubeTeleporter.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Cube Teleporter]]''
The Cube teleporter is a feature unlocked by multiple upgrades. It allows the player to teleport to different zones of the game.

=== Terriac de Scripta ===

[[File:Terriac_de_Scripta.png|200px|thumb|right]]
:''Main article: [[Paper Dimension]]''
:''Terriac de Scripta&lt;br&gt; In Memoriam, Terriac Papere Orbis&lt;br&gt; - MCMXVII -''&lt;br&gt;
The text above is written in Latin which roughly translates to:&lt;br&gt;

:''Terriac the scripter&lt;br&gt; In memory of Terriac Paper World&lt;br&gt; - 1917 -''

Going into the painting teleports the player to the [[Paper Dimension]].


== History ==
=== v1.0 ===
* There used to be a Buymax upgrade next to {{Upgrade|#1αb|NJUT}} (The stud tower) to buy max the upgrade. It got removed in 1.1 because it was causing {{Upgrade|#1αb|NJUT}} automation to not work correctly.

== Trivia ==
* Before release, the {{Baseplate|Bonus}} underwent many design and color changes, like green, yellow, blue(?), red and even yellow again then back to green. It also used to be ocean-themed.
* There used to be a mechanic where the player had to change their display name to what was according to the list, and it would boost their credits gain in some way. However, it was scrapped because:
** ''"The idea was just stupid"'' 
** It broke the rule of Bonus progression not influencing Main progression.

